{
  "name": "ok_file_write",
  "description": "file/write, the record that a person saved a buffer through the editor. It is not a tool/call: the tool channel answers the model, and a human save has no model in the loop. The row exists because after a restart the file on disk is the only surviving evidence of it, and a reader that finds the disk disagreeing with an earlier fs_read should be able to say when and by whom the file last changed. Payload is {path, bytes, sha256}; the digest is of the bytes written, so a later reader can tell whether the file still matches what was saved. `path` is workspace-relative and never absolute.",
